+# Deployment
+
+Fizzy ships with a [Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org/) configuration for a
+single Linux server. The app, its SQLite databases, Active Storage files, cache,
+cable, and background jobs all run from one container. [kamal-proxy](https://github.com/basecamp/kamal-proxy)
+terminates TLS and obtains a Let's Encrypt certificate for your hostname.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- A Linux server with Docker installed and ports 80 and 443 open.
+- A DNS record for your hostname pointing at the server.
+- SSH access to the server. The default Kamal user is `root`; if you use another
+  user, add an `ssh.user` setting to `config/deploy.yml`.
+- Docker installed on the machine where you run Kamal. Kamal uses a local
+  registry on that machine, so you do not need a Docker Hub or GHCR account.
+
+## Configure
+
+Edit `config/deploy.yml` and replace:
+
+1. The `servers.web` address (`192.0.2.1`) with your server's SSH host or IP.
+2. Both occurrences of `fizzy.example.com` with the hostname whose DNS points at
+   the server. One is used by the proxy for TLS and routing; the other is
+   `APP_HOST`, which is used to generate links in emails and the app.
+3. The SMTP settings (`SMTP_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_PORT`, `SMTP_USERNAME`) with the
+   details for your mail server.
+4. `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS` with the address you want Fizzy email to come from.
+
+If your server is ARM-based, change `builder.arch` from `amd64` to `arm64`.
+
+The defaults assume SMTP over port 587 with STARTTLS. If your provider uses
+implicit TLS on port 465, also add these to the `env.clear` section:
+
+```yaml
+    SMTP_TLS: "true"
+    SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO: "false"
+```
+
+Set `SMTP_AUTHENTICATION` if your mail server uses a value other than `plain`
+(for example, `login`). If your mail server does not require authentication, leave
+`SMTP_USERNAME` empty; authentication is then omitted.
+
+## Secrets
+
+Generate a secret key base once and store it in your password manager. Reuse
+the same value for every deploy so existing sessions and signed URLs remain
+valid:
+
+```sh
+export SECRET_KEY_BASE="$(bin/rails secret)"
+export SMTP_PASSWORD="your-smtp-password"
+```
+
+The `.kamal/secrets` file reads both values from your shell and passes them to
+the container. If you keep secrets in files or a password manager instead, edit
+`.kamal/secrets` to read them from there. Do not commit actual secret values.
+
+If you use Rails encrypted credentials, uncomment the `RAILS_MASTER_KEY` line in
+`.kamal/secrets` and add `RAILS_MASTER_KEY` to the `env.secret` list in
+`config/deploy.yml`.
+
+## Deploy
+
+The first deploy builds the image, starts the proxy, creates the database, and
+starts the app:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal setup
+```
+
+Once DNS has propagated and the certificate has been issued, Fizzy will be
+available at `https://your-hostname`.
+
+Subsequent deploys use:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal deploy
+```
+
+The container entrypoint runs `bin/rails db:prepare` before the server starts,
+so new migrations are applied automatically on every deploy.
+
+## Data and background jobs
+
+Kamal mounts the named `fizzy_storage` volume at `/rails/storage`. That single
+directory contains the production SQLite databases, the Solid Queue/Cache/Cable
+databases, and locally stored uploads. It is not replaced when the container is
+replaced, so data survives deployments.
+
+Do not run `bin/kamal remove` unless you intend to delete the application
+containers and volume. Back up the volume (or at least `/rails/storage`) along
+with any data you cannot afford to lose.
+
+Solid Queue runs inside the web container via its Puma plugin. There is no
+separate worker host to deploy or monitor. `WEB_CONCURRENCY` and
+`JOB_CONCURRENCY` are both set to `1` in `config/deploy.yml` to keep the
+footprint and SQLite contention appropriate for a single box.
+
+## Useful commands
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal logs -f      # Follow application logs
+bin/kamal console      # Open a Rails console in the running container
+bin/kamal shell        # Open a shell in the running container
+bin/kamal dbc          # Open a SQLite console
+```
